{
  "about": "How bottles are listed and which one Put Away places, shared by CaveKit (BottlePlaceTests.swift) and the Android core (BottlePlaceTest.kt). All bottles are of one wine and in the cellar. A bottle with 'rack' has that position (row, column, depth default 0). placeOrder is Cellar.inPlaceOrder: storages in their order, then shelf (wine fridge with layers) or row, depth front first, layer from the bottom, position; bottles without a position last, oldest first (addedAt), then by id compared as text ignoring case. putAway is bottleToPutAway: among bottles without a position, one not kept for an occasion first, then the oldest, then by id; null when every bottle has a position. openOn is the storage the Move sheet opens on for the putAway bottle (storageToOpen): for a bottle out of storage, the one holding most bottles of its wine (the first in order on a tie), else preferred (the last storage used on the device, null in these vectors) while it has a free position, else the one with most free positions (the first on a tie); null when there is no storage or no bottle to put away.",
